i.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sudhakarsingh27","id":4879686,"login":"sudhakarsingh27","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4Nzk2ODY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudhakarsingh27","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"> @sudhakarsingh27 id should be stable, how do you intend to use process_index ?\r\n\r\n@zhangqiaorjc There was some confusion when we're looking at how shards are assigned to GPUs with GDAs since the process-GPU mapping was random (so to fix that, we need to do pass the mesh of devices sorted by their GPU ids instead of `process_index`).\r\n\r\nThe other potential problem is that if process-GPU mapping is random, then it's possible that some array might get sharded across hosts (nodes) instead of within the node. Having deterministic 1:1 mapping might prevent that from happening? ","created_at":"2022-09-30T20:35:22Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/12570#issuecomment-1263999876","id":1263999876,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/12570","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5LVxuE","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1263999876/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-09-30T20:35:38Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1263999876","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/